                             |CKBChapter 3 - Combat
                     |BKB----------------------------------------

|YKOStart a fight with |YKBkill <target>|YKO. Before attacking, use
|YKBassess <target>|YKO for a rough comparison and read room descriptions
for warnings. Some monsters are aggressive and attack as soon as you enter.

Every combat round contains one or more independent swings. A swing may
critically hit, hit, be dodged, be absorbed, or miss. Weapon size, speed,
accuracy, your stats, training, armour, resistances, and guild or class
abilities all matter.

Watch your resources with |YKBmonitor bar|YKO, |YKBmon|YKO, or
|YKB.|YKO. Set |YKBwimpy <percent>|YKO to flee automatically at low health;
you can also flee by moving through an exit. Use |YKBassist <player>|YKO to
join a friend's fight without accidentally targeting the friend.

New characters can use |YKBnheal|YKO, |YKBnbolt|YKO, |YKBnkick|YKO,
|YKBnpunch|YKO, and
|YKBncot|YKO through level 5. Their adventurer forms
|YKBaheal|YKO, |YKBabolt|YKO, |YKBakick|YKO, |YKBapunch|YKO, and
|YKBacot|YKO remain
available from levels 6 through 49.

Use |YKBcombatbrief|YKO to control routine combat text. The short, self, hit,
and damage options remain independent. |YKBcombatbrief visual|YKO moves
routine swings into Darkflow's Combat pane when that pane is ready; important
warnings, ability results, fleeing, death, and rewards remain in the terminal.

After combat, recover with rest, food, drink, potions, or guild abilities.
Do not attack another player's target without permission: kill stealing is
against the rules.|000

